



      2 T      olive oil
      6 cloves garlic
      2 T      ginger
      1        jalapeno pepper
      1 T      salt
      3/4 t    cayenne pepper
      4 lbs    butternut squash cut into
                  2" cubes
      3 c      broth
      1 T      brown sugar   
      3 T      whipping cream

      Brown the squash in a skillet with everything
      above it in the appropriate way.  Add broth 
      and simmer till squash is tender.  Puree, 
      strain, and serve garnished with creme fraiche


      1     leek (8 oz)
      2 T   butter 
      8 oz  carrots
      4 oz  celery
      1/2 c chopped onion
      1     clove garlic
                      --- saute until onion is limp
      2 q. chix broth
      4 c   mashed pumpkin
      1/2 c apple cider
      8 oz  apple
      2 t   chopped ginger
      1/2 t cinnamon
      1/8 t allspice
                      --- add, boil, puree

      garnish with creme fraiche and lemon  zest

      mashed pumpkin: slice in half, rub with
      butter, bake 45 - 75 minutes until soft.
      yield 3/4 - 5/4 c per lb raw



      Cream of Pumpkin Soup

      3     T butter
      1     large onion diced (1 cup)
      5     cloves garlic
      .5 t  crushed red pepper
      1 qt  chicken broth
      .75 c wild rice
      1.5 c .5 & .5
      1 T   flour
      3 C   pumpkin

      Melt bugger, cook onion & garlic till tender.
      Add pepper, cook 1 min more.  Add broth, bring
      to boil.  Add wild rice, simmer 40 min till
      tender.  Mix 1/2+1/2 with flour, add to soup
      along with pumpkin.  Simmer 15 minutes, 
      puree with hand blender, run through soup
      mill.